1
00:00:06,156 --> 00:00:09,659
Heiwa Fansubs Presents:
Great Detective Conan
Challenge to Kudo Shin'ichi

2
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:11,328
Shin'ichi!

3
00:00:11,628 --> 00:00:13,830
Ran! Damn!

4
00:00:14,031 --> 00:00:14,998
Ran!

5
00:00:15,399 --> 00:00:16,500
Shin'ichi!

6
00:00:16,666 --> 00:00:17,768
Shin'ichi!

7
00:00:17,801 --> 00:00:20,303
Type in the password once more.

8
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:34,985
Shin'ichi?

9
00:00:35,052 --> 00:00:36,787
Ran, are you okay?

10
00:00:36,887 --> 00:00:38,555
Shin'ichi!

11
00:00:38,655 --> 00:00:40,524
Shin'ichi, save me!

12
00:00:40,557 --> 00:00:42,159
Save me...

13
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:54,404
Stop!

14
00:00:54,805 --> 00:00:56,873
You thought you could run away from me?

15
00:00:58,075 --> 00:01:00,377
Stop! Don't come near me!

16
00:01:05,115 --> 00:01:07,150
You thought you'd make a fool of me!?

17
00:01:12,622 --> 00:01:14,624
You deceived me, you rascal...

18
00:01:21,898 --> 00:01:24,134
That's DV, isn't it?
(domestic violence)

19
00:01:26,803 --> 00:01:29,005
"Client
Mizutani Yukino"

20
00:01:29,172 --> 00:01:32,709
I... might be killed by him.

21
00:01:32,776 --> 00:01:33,844
Eh?!

22
00:01:33,910 --> 00:01:38,148
"She's a client of Dad's, Mizutani Yukino-san."

23
00:01:38,248 --> 00:01:42,385
"She's been receiving DV and being stalked
by her lover, Kubo Shunsuke."

24
00:01:42,552 --> 00:01:46,656
"She had made an appointment with Dad
to consult with him over a video chat line."

25
00:01:47,824 --> 00:01:48,892
"Even so..."

26
00:01:49,092 --> 00:01:52,662
"...since he suddenly decided to go see
the Idol Okino Yoko-san's concert instead..."

27
00:01:52,863 --> 00:01:55,265
"...I ended up going to the video chat."

28
00:02:01,204 --> 00:02:03,406
What should I do about this?

29
00:02:05,542 --> 00:02:09,846
I think he's watching me from somewhere.

30
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:12,115
I'm too scared to leave this apartment.

31
00:02:12,349 --> 00:02:16,753
And this is why you were
video chatting with my Dad, isn't it?

32
00:02:18,555 --> 00:02:21,424
Truth is, I live in the neighborhood.

33
00:02:21,525 --> 00:02:24,227
Beika Apartments, room 301.

34
00:02:24,461 --> 00:02:25,962
Ah, there.

35
00:02:26,496 --> 00:02:30,967
I've had a bad feeling all of today.

36
00:02:33,937 --> 00:02:35,472
He's come! It's Kubo!

37
00:02:39,075 --> 00:02:42,045
Mizutani-san, you absolutely mustn't leave.

38
00:02:44,147 --> 00:02:45,715
I'll report this to the police.

39
00:02:45,782 --> 00:02:49,286
Don't! If you do that, I don't know what
revenge he'll take against me.

40
00:02:49,619 --> 00:02:52,889
Then, what should we do?

41
00:02:54,925 --> 00:02:56,326
Mizutani-san!

42
00:02:56,493 --> 00:02:58,762
You mustn't leave there!

43
00:02:59,396 --> 00:03:00,764
Stop!

44
00:03:00,897 --> 00:03:03,066
You thought you could run away, huh?

45
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:04,668
Mizutani-san!

46
00:03:04,901 --> 00:03:06,203
Mizutani-san!?

47
00:03:06,236 --> 00:03:09,172
Kyaa! Save me!

48
00:03:12,976 --> 00:03:15,979
Mizutani-san, are you okay?!

49
00:03:21,218 --> 00:03:22,719
It couldn't be...

50
00:03:29,125 --> 00:03:31,194
Hello, Shin'ichi?
There's been an incident.

51
00:03:31,261 --> 00:03:33,396
Come to the Beika Apartments right away.

52
00:03:42,405 --> 00:03:43,673
"Stop!"

53
00:03:45,008 --> 00:03:47,110
"You thought you could run away, huh?"

54
00:03:47,277 --> 00:03:50,647
"Don't! Don't come near me!"

55
00:03:51,715 --> 00:03:52,949
"Stop!"

56
00:04:04,127 --> 00:04:04,828
"Beika Apartments"

57
00:04:06,062 --> 00:04:07,964
Ah, I'm sorry!

58
00:04:22,712 --> 00:04:24,180
Mizutani-san!

59
00:04:26,650 --> 00:04:28,451
Mizutani-san!

60
00:04:38,094 --> 00:04:39,863
Mizutani-san?

61
00:04:49,272 --> 00:04:51,074
Mizutani-san...

62
00:04:57,681 --> 00:04:59,115
"Beika Apartments"

63
00:05:00,817 --> 00:05:03,553
When you were video chatting
with Mizutani Yukino-san...

64
00:05:03,620 --> 00:05:06,189
...this man "Kubo" attacked her?

65
00:05:06,389 --> 00:05:08,024
What does Kubo look like?

66
00:05:08,358 --> 00:05:13,096
Well, um... thing is...
He never appeared on-screen.

67
00:05:13,196 --> 00:05:14,331
You didn't see him?

68
00:05:14,431 --> 00:05:17,767
Then you didn't see either
the criminal's face nor what happened?

69
00:05:17,834 --> 00:05:21,237
But I heard her screaming, "Kubo-san, don't!"

70
00:05:21,438 --> 00:05:24,040
I found this discarded in the trash.

71
00:05:27,677 --> 00:05:31,548
Ah! That's the one!
He must be Kubo!

72
00:05:31,648 --> 00:05:33,116
Huh? But you said
you didn't see him, didn't you?

73
00:05:33,216 --> 00:05:35,552
I bumped into this man down
at the entrance hallway.

74
00:05:35,618 --> 00:05:36,686
"I'm sorry!"

75
00:05:37,053 --> 00:05:39,889
Mizutani-san told me how he had
used violence on her many times.

76
00:05:40,123 --> 00:05:42,525
Maybe he's even killed her!

77
00:05:42,625 --> 00:05:46,863
We can't conclude that is a
murder incident from just a few bloodstains.

78
00:05:47,197 --> 00:05:48,832
No...

79
00:05:48,898 --> 00:05:50,834
This was just a couple's dispute, wasn't it?

80
00:05:50,967 --> 00:05:54,003
Shin'ichi! Say something!

81
00:05:54,871 --> 00:05:58,508
Was she really chatting to you from here?

82
00:05:58,975 --> 00:06:01,411
Eh? What do you mean?

83
00:06:02,645 --> 00:06:04,614
The chat software hasn't been started.

84
00:06:04,748 --> 00:06:06,850
If she had been chatting with Ran
when she was attacked...

85
00:06:06,950 --> 00:06:10,587
...it should still be showing the Internet cafe
you left to come here.

86
00:06:11,354 --> 00:06:12,589
I see.

87
00:06:12,822 --> 00:06:15,658
Mizutani-san was definitely in this room!

88
00:06:15,759 --> 00:06:20,096
These are the red curtains
I saw behind Mizutani-san.

89
00:06:21,131 --> 00:06:22,866
I'm not mistaken!

90
00:06:26,970 --> 00:06:27,737
Ran.

91
00:06:27,804 --> 00:06:31,074
At the time you bumped into this Kubo,
was there anyone else around?

92
00:06:31,174 --> 00:06:33,076
No, he was alone.

93
00:06:33,910 --> 00:06:38,181
If it's as Ran says,
and that Kubo-san attacked Mizutani-san here...

94
00:06:43,219 --> 00:06:46,856
...then she would most likely still be
somewhere here in this apartment building.

95
00:06:47,757 --> 00:06:51,628
She would most likely still be
somewhere here in this apartment building.

96
00:06:52,829 --> 00:06:55,465
This incident occurred at 8:16.

97
00:06:55,765 --> 00:06:57,367
"Mizutani-san!"

98
00:06:57,634 --> 00:07:00,437
"Kyaa! Save me!"

99
00:07:00,537 --> 00:07:03,206
Ran arrived here at 8:31.

100
00:07:03,306 --> 00:07:05,208
The time in-between was only 15 minutes.

101
00:07:05,308 --> 00:07:07,577
Even if Mizutani-san is a small person...

102
00:07:07,644 --> 00:07:10,980
...for a murderer to forcibly tie her up
and take her away in just 15 minutes...

103
00:07:11,147 --> 00:07:14,884
...the distance he would be able
to take her would be limited.

104
00:07:15,051 --> 00:07:19,823
What's more, the only person who exited the
apartment complex during that time was that man.

105
00:07:20,256 --> 00:07:22,358
If he had attempted to move
Mizutani-san in that condition...

106
00:07:22,425 --> 00:07:24,794
...he would have been captured on
the surveillance video.

107
00:07:25,795 --> 00:07:29,199
Please rescue Mizutani-san!
It may already be too late.

108
00:07:29,632 --> 00:07:31,901
Detective Sato!

109
00:07:33,937 --> 00:07:36,873
- Check every room in the complex.
- Yes!

110
00:07:41,377 --> 00:07:43,913
Detective Sato...

111
00:07:44,314 --> 00:07:45,482
"Still..."

112
00:07:45,648 --> 00:07:49,052
"...Mizutani Yukino-san
was nowhere to be found."

113
00:07:53,056 --> 00:07:54,924
"And then, 6 hours later..."

114
00:07:55,058 --> 00:07:57,093
"...the case took an entirely
different direction."

115
00:07:57,126 --> 00:07:58,094
"Saitama Weekly Apartments"

116
00:07:58,895 --> 00:08:00,597
"Mizutani Yukino-san's body..."

117
00:08:00,797 --> 00:08:05,068
"...was found in the room of
a weekly apartment in Saitama."

118
00:08:05,168 --> 00:08:06,769
"Stop, Kubo-san!"

119
00:08:08,638 --> 00:08:09,873
"Save me!"

120
00:08:11,441 --> 00:08:13,376
Mizutani-san...

121
00:08:15,378 --> 00:08:17,747
Around 2:00am...

122
00:08:17,847 --> 00:08:22,585
...the Manager was making his rounds and,
seeing the door was open, discovered the corpse.

123
00:08:22,785 --> 00:08:27,924
From the condition of the corpse, the estimated
time of death was between 8:00pm to 8:30pm.

124
00:08:28,892 --> 00:08:31,995
That was the time when
Mizutani-san and I were chatting!

125
00:08:32,295 --> 00:08:37,000
The cause of death was a sharp knife stuck
into her abdomen, causing excessive bleeding.

126
00:08:37,267 --> 00:08:40,169
On the rug there are massive bloodstains.

127
00:08:40,303 --> 00:08:43,540
Therefore the local Saitama police concluded
she had been stabbed to death here.

128
00:08:43,706 --> 00:08:45,408
She was killed here?!

129
00:08:45,508 --> 00:08:46,543
That couldn't be!

130
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:50,013
Mizutani-san was chatting with me
from her Beika Apartment, after all!

131
00:08:53,316 --> 00:08:54,684
Ran.

132
00:08:59,556 --> 00:09:02,959
Ah! Right, right,
this was where Mizutani-san was.

133
00:09:03,326 --> 00:09:06,029
This is... from over here.

134
00:09:06,262 --> 00:09:07,597
Eh?

135
00:09:09,899 --> 00:09:11,868
This apartment has been arranged with...

136
00:09:12,101 --> 00:09:15,605
...the same background trick as the one
over at the Beika Apartments during your chat.

137
00:09:16,072 --> 00:09:18,074
What is this about?

138
00:09:18,207 --> 00:09:20,610
In other words, we don't really know...

139
00:09:20,777 --> 00:09:24,714
...which apartment Mizutani-san
was chatting from, the Beika Apartment...

140
00:09:24,714 --> 00:09:26,449
...or here from the Saitama apartment.

141
00:09:26,482 --> 00:09:28,885
But, judging from the situation here...

142
00:09:28,952 --> 00:09:31,688
...it's right to think she was
killed here, isn't it?

143
00:09:31,921 --> 00:09:36,926
The results of the investigation prove the blood
in these stains was from Mizutani Yukino-san.

144
00:09:38,761 --> 00:09:39,896
"Stop!"

145
00:09:40,797 --> 00:09:42,732
If she was in this apartment...

146
00:09:42,865 --> 00:09:45,735
...then the line that Kubo-san
is the murderer disappears.

147
00:09:46,169 --> 00:09:50,039
Why?!
She was screaming, "Stop it, Kubo-san!"

148
00:09:50,306 --> 00:09:54,110
The distance from this apartment in Saitama
to the one in Beika is approximately 120 km.

149
00:09:54,377 --> 00:09:56,245
It takes 3 hours to drive here.

150
00:09:56,446 --> 00:09:59,082
To get here, where Mizutani-san was killed...

151
00:09:59,148 --> 00:10:02,885
...to the Beika Apartments hallway where
Ran bumped into him only 15 minutes later...

152
00:10:02,986 --> 00:10:04,887
...would be physically impossible.

153
00:10:06,055 --> 00:10:09,092
If Kubo-san isn't the murderer...

154
00:10:09,892 --> 00:10:12,028
Then did I hear it wrong?

155
00:10:12,161 --> 00:10:13,663
Detective Sato!

156
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:17,767
We've discovered the victim's passport
and an airline boarding pass for today.

157
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:19,235
Thank you.

158
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:23,539
It's for Singapore, taking off at 6:25.

159
00:10:23,606 --> 00:10:25,842
It's a one-way ticket.

160
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:30,847
She was thinking of getting away from
Kubo-san and making a fresh start in life.

161
00:10:32,515 --> 00:10:35,284
Kudo-kun, is something bothering you?

162
00:10:35,652 --> 00:10:40,990
Even if she was here hiding out from Kubo-san
until she could run off to a foreign country...

163
00:10:41,624 --> 00:10:46,729
...why would she decorate this apartment
to match the one in the Beika Apartment complex?

164
00:10:47,964 --> 00:10:50,833
When did she start renting this apartment?

165
00:10:50,967 --> 00:10:56,005
According to the manager, Mizutani Yukino-san
booked it a week ago over the Internet.

166
00:10:56,239 --> 00:10:58,007
An Internet reservation...

167
00:10:58,207 --> 00:11:00,410
A week ago...

168
00:11:00,510 --> 00:11:01,711
That's right!

169
00:11:01,878 --> 00:11:04,113
I found this at home.

170
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:07,083
Here.

171
00:11:08,317 --> 00:11:09,619
This is...

172
00:11:09,719 --> 00:11:12,455
Ah, this cabbage is really cheap, isn't it?

173
00:11:13,022 --> 00:11:14,457
Not that!

174
00:11:14,857 --> 00:11:15,992
This!

175
00:11:16,359 --> 00:11:21,030
"July 20th, phone consultation with Mizutani Yukino.
Stalker and DV victim."

176
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:24,834
"July 24th. Talked for 1 hour
by video chat from 9:30 pm."

177
00:11:24,867 --> 00:11:30,373
"July 24th. 7:00pm, said she was afraid
of Kubo and cried. Cried during the video chat."

178
00:11:30,473 --> 00:11:33,142
"Not being able to hold her
by the shoulders is irritating."

179
00:11:33,543 --> 00:11:36,813
"Our next video chat
will be at 8:00 pm on the 27th."

180
00:11:37,513 --> 00:11:39,482
This are Detective Mori's memos, aren't they?

181
00:11:39,615 --> 00:11:43,252
The first time she and Ran's old man
had a consultations was on July 20th.

182
00:11:43,319 --> 00:11:44,854
That was exactly one week ago.

183
00:11:45,421 --> 00:11:50,259
I wonder what detective work she
asked Ran's father do in the first place?

184
00:11:50,626 --> 00:11:52,061
Yukino!

185
00:11:52,161 --> 00:11:53,362
Yukino!

186
00:11:53,429 --> 00:11:55,364
- It's Kubo...
- Yukino!

187
00:11:55,431 --> 00:11:57,366
Please stop!

188
00:12:02,505 --> 00:12:04,907
Yukino is...

189
00:12:08,177 --> 00:12:10,646
Has she really been killed?

190
00:12:10,947 --> 00:12:12,815
Who on earth would do that...

191
00:12:16,419 --> 00:12:18,588
Kubo Kensuke-san?

192
00:12:18,688 --> 00:12:23,593
You and Mizutani Yukino-san were
talking about separating, weren't you?

193
00:12:23,693 --> 00:12:26,562
"Yukino's Lover - Kubo Kensuke"
Are you suspicious of me?

194
00:12:27,230 --> 00:12:28,898
I loved her!

195
00:12:28,965 --> 00:12:30,032
You're lying!

196
00:12:30,099 --> 00:12:32,635
You used violence against her, didn't you?

197
00:12:32,735 --> 00:12:36,639
It looked like her face was injured and I also heard
her painful screams of "Please don't, please don't!"

198
00:12:36,706 --> 00:12:38,641
I'm not lying!

199
00:12:39,275 --> 00:12:41,644
I'm the victim.

200
00:12:41,778 --> 00:12:45,081
She was originally in charge of
my brokerage firm...

201
00:12:46,716 --> 00:12:49,085
...but she took my money away
by deception.

202
00:12:49,118 --> 00:12:50,153
You'll know if you check into it...

203
00:12:50,153 --> 00:12:50,987
Liar!

204
00:12:51,053 --> 00:12:53,055
She also said you were stalking her.

205
00:12:53,156 --> 00:12:56,726
You knowing about this Weekly Apartment
itself is evidence enough that you're a stalker!

206
00:12:56,859 --> 00:12:58,961
It's true I was stalking Yukino.

207
00:13:00,062 --> 00:13:01,898
"What should I do about this?"

208
00:13:02,732 --> 00:13:07,370
It was because 60 million yen had
disappeared from my bank account.

209
00:13:07,570 --> 00:13:11,674
So I looked for her in order
to get it back somehow.

210
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:15,077
I also knew about the existence of
this apartment 5 days ago.

211
00:13:16,012 --> 00:13:17,980
At half past 8 this evening...

212
00:13:18,147 --> 00:13:20,383
...you were in the Beika Apartment
complex, weren't you?

213
00:13:20,516 --> 00:13:21,684
What were you doing?

214
00:13:21,717 --> 00:13:24,654
I told you; I went to talk to her
about the money.

215
00:13:25,254 --> 00:13:27,790
I thought if she apologized...

216
00:13:28,257 --> 00:13:29,792
...I'd forgive her.

217
00:13:29,992 --> 00:13:31,994
I really did love her.

218
00:13:35,298 --> 00:13:38,501
Did you meet with Mizutani-san?

219
00:13:39,202 --> 00:13:41,037
She wasn't in.

220
00:13:42,371 --> 00:13:48,110
So when I had no choice but to go home,
that's when I bumped into this girl in the hallway.

221
00:13:48,644 --> 00:13:50,112
You're lying.

222
00:13:50,346 --> 00:13:52,415
You killed her!

223
00:13:52,548 --> 00:13:56,352
You'd know best that it would
have been impossible for me to kill her!

224
00:13:58,321 --> 00:14:00,289
It was... ESP!

225
00:14:00,423 --> 00:14:03,526
I'm sure you could move her
in an instant with ESP, couldn't you!?

226
00:14:03,593 --> 00:14:05,127
What are you talking about?

227
00:14:05,228 --> 00:14:06,696
But...

228
00:14:08,030 --> 00:14:13,202
Can you say there was another man
whom Mizutani Yukino-san was seeing?

229
00:14:13,569 --> 00:14:15,705
There might have been.

230
00:14:16,472 --> 00:14:19,475
You mean a love-triangle?

231
00:14:19,942 --> 00:14:22,178
Why do you think that?

232
00:14:22,445 --> 00:14:24,313
After all, she was beautiful...

233
00:14:24,413 --> 00:14:26,315
...and now that the line
to Kubo-san has disappeared...

234
00:14:26,382 --> 00:14:31,387
...isn't it natural to consider the possibility she'd
have another man bearing a grudge against her?

235
00:14:31,888 --> 00:14:34,790
Another man, huh?

236
00:14:35,324 --> 00:14:38,194
Another...

237
00:14:49,605 --> 00:14:53,075
It originally occurred
at totally different place!

238
00:14:53,576 --> 00:14:56,512
Huh? Have you figured it out?

239
00:14:57,013 --> 00:14:59,382
Shin'ichi? Tell us.

240
00:14:59,815 --> 00:15:01,918
There is only one truth.

241
00:15:02,018 --> 00:15:03,886
That is...

242
00:15:04,553 --> 00:15:07,156
...a love triangle.

243
00:15:08,824 --> 00:15:12,762
Huh? What's that?
Who's the criminal?

244
00:15:12,862 --> 00:15:14,764
The criminal is...

245
00:15:16,532 --> 00:15:18,701
Kubo-san, please go home.

246
00:15:19,402 --> 00:15:21,237
Where's your home?

247
00:15:21,470 --> 00:15:23,239
Matoiwa, but...

248
00:15:23,406 --> 00:15:25,408
That's about 2 hours away, isn't it?

249
00:15:26,108 --> 00:15:27,510
Please take him home by police car.

250
00:15:27,610 --> 00:15:31,247
Shin'ichi!
This guy's definitely the killer!

251
00:15:38,688 --> 00:15:42,291
What do you mean the truth
is about a love triangle?

252
00:15:42,491 --> 00:15:45,594
This doesn't consist of just two of them.

253
00:15:46,062 --> 00:15:48,631
Eh? What's that?

254
00:15:48,698 --> 00:15:53,302
Tell me how that's connected
to this incident! Shin'ichi!

255
00:16:10,686 --> 00:16:12,488
"Incoming Video Chat call from Shin'ichi Kudo"

256
00:16:13,756 --> 00:16:17,059
I'm sorry.
I forgot to ask you something.

257
00:16:18,194 --> 00:16:20,463
Is it okay to talk about it using video chat?

258
00:16:20,563 --> 00:16:23,466
Well truth is, this came out.

259
00:16:23,899 --> 00:16:25,968
It's a fingerprint from the crime scene.

260
00:16:26,235 --> 00:16:30,139
They said they were luckily able to pull this
from off of Mizutani Yukino-san's clothes.

261
00:16:30,439 --> 00:16:32,375
And, sorry to trouble you...

262
00:16:32,475 --> 00:16:35,611
...but I wanted to confirm with you
that this isn't your fingerprint.

263
00:16:35,945 --> 00:16:40,016
After that, there was something like
a character written on the rug.

264
00:16:40,216 --> 00:16:44,320
Would you have some idea of
Mizutani Yukino-san's way of writing?

265
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:48,491
I've taken a photo of it,
so if you could take a look at it.

266
00:16:48,891 --> 00:16:52,261
I think the detectives are
on their way out there now.

267
00:16:52,528 --> 00:16:56,265
Let's see...
Could you wait there for 2 hours?

268
00:16:57,133 --> 00:16:59,502
All right. I'll be waiting.

269
00:17:18,454 --> 00:17:20,022
Kubo-san.

270
00:17:22,191 --> 00:17:25,327
It seems we arrived
a little sooner than you thought.

271
00:17:25,861 --> 00:17:27,329
Ho... how...

272
00:17:27,530 --> 00:17:29,965
We did it the same way you did.

273
00:17:31,801 --> 00:17:35,938
The criminal is you, isn't it,
Kubo Kensuke-san?

274
00:17:37,907 --> 00:17:39,442
What do you mean?

275
00:17:40,109 --> 00:17:44,046
The color of the doors at those
Weekly Apartments in Saitama are an olive green.

276
00:17:44,180 --> 00:17:48,184
So, when you saw me standing in front of
an olive green door...

277
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:54,223
...Kubo-san, you simply believed I was still at
those Weekly Apartments in Saitama.

278
00:17:55,157 --> 00:17:56,625
But...

279
00:17:58,727 --> 00:18:01,497
Truth is, I was nearby.

280
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:15,177
Colors and shapes make
the greatest impression on the brain...

281
00:18:15,277 --> 00:18:17,179
It remembers those sorts of things.

282
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:20,349
Kudo-kun, please explain this clearly.

283
00:18:20,483 --> 00:18:24,386
If Mizutani-san had been killed
in those Weekly Apartments in Saitama...

284
00:18:24,587 --> 00:18:26,455
...it would have been impossible for Kubo-san...

285
00:18:26,555 --> 00:18:30,259
...who was at the Beika Apartments,
to have committed the crime in those 15 minutes.

286
00:18:30,459 --> 00:18:36,298
It takes 3 hours by car to get to the Weekly
Apartments from the Beika Apartments, doesn't it?

287
00:18:36,632 --> 00:18:42,404
In truth, she was killed within a range of
15 minutes from the Beika Apartments.

288
00:18:42,671 --> 00:18:44,173
In other words...

289
00:18:45,608 --> 00:18:47,676
Like this.

290
00:18:48,577 --> 00:18:50,246
Oh, Ran-chan!

291
00:18:50,312 --> 00:18:51,847
Where are you right now?

292
00:18:51,914 --> 00:18:55,217
The Weekly Apartments in Saitama?
Or else at the Beika Apartment complex?

293
00:18:55,384 --> 00:18:56,919
I'm at neither.

294
00:18:56,986 --> 00:18:58,387
Eh?

295
00:18:58,888 --> 00:19:01,257
There was a third apartment.

296
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:06,662
That was where you killed her,
wasn't it, Kubo-san?

297
00:19:16,372 --> 00:19:17,907
Huh?

298
00:19:18,274 --> 00:19:20,309
This has the same interior?

299
00:19:20,409 --> 00:19:21,377
Yes.

300
00:19:21,443 --> 00:19:24,013
In other words, three apartments that
would appear the same on the video chat...

301
00:19:24,046 --> 00:19:25,014
"Beika Apartments
Saitama Weekly Apartments - Third Apartment"

302
00:19:25,047 --> 00:19:28,150
You could say there were 3 different places.

303
00:19:30,786 --> 00:19:33,255
Why would he do such a thing?

304
00:19:34,957 --> 00:19:39,094
It's true that Mizutani-san
cheated you out of the 60 million yen.

305
00:19:39,228 --> 00:19:43,399
Furthermore, she planned to make it seem
as if you had murdered her...

306
00:19:43,499 --> 00:19:46,702
...and would then run off to a foreign country.

307
00:19:47,303 --> 00:19:50,072
She was a terrible woman.

308
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:55,477
In order to have someone who could testify to
her situation and that she had been killed...

309
00:19:56,011 --> 00:19:58,614
...she got in touch with
Ran's father by video chat.

310
00:19:58,981 --> 00:20:02,318
The main point though is that Ran's father
went to a live concert instead.

311
00:20:02,585 --> 00:20:06,488
Then, what were those screams I heard?

312
00:20:07,756 --> 00:20:09,425
This.

313
00:20:12,328 --> 00:20:13,762
"Stop!"

314
00:20:18,067 --> 00:20:20,236
Most likely this recording...

315
00:20:21,937 --> 00:20:23,572
Was a recording from the time when...

316
00:20:23,672 --> 00:20:26,875
...Kubo-san stormed over to
Mizutani-san's apartment to complain, wasn't it?

317
00:20:27,343 --> 00:20:30,379
"This is all a misunderstanding."

318
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:35,851
"Stop."

319
00:20:37,353 --> 00:20:38,721
"Stop it!"

320
00:20:38,988 --> 00:20:41,390
"You thought you could run away from me?"

321
00:20:42,057 --> 00:20:44,293
"You thought you'd made a fool of me!"

322
00:20:49,031 --> 00:20:52,301
What she then played back to Ran was...

323
00:20:53,469 --> 00:20:55,104
"Mizutani-san!"

324
00:20:55,204 --> 00:20:57,406
"You shouldn't go out!"

325
00:20:57,973 --> 00:20:59,041
"Stop!"

326
00:20:59,074 --> 00:21:01,043
"You thought you'd make a fool of me!?"

327
00:21:01,310 --> 00:21:03,445
"You deceived me! You rascal!"

328
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:06,248
"Mizutani-san!"

329
00:21:06,649 --> 00:21:08,250
"Mizutani-san!"

330
00:21:08,517 --> 00:21:09,285
"Mizutani-san!"

331
00:21:09,318 --> 00:21:13,222
She made Ran believe she was being
attacked during the video chat.

332
00:21:13,422 --> 00:21:15,224
I was tricked by that woman!

333
00:21:15,391 --> 00:21:17,793
Then, there wasn't any DV?

334
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:20,896
But Shin'ichi, how did you figure out
she was putting on an act?

335
00:21:20,996 --> 00:21:24,066
Ah, that was from the gauze.

336
00:21:24,233 --> 00:21:26,735
"It looked like she'd been hurt on her face."

337
00:21:27,636 --> 00:21:32,308
But, after she was killed,
there wasn't a wound on her face.

338
00:21:33,976 --> 00:21:37,313
I was totally tricked.

339
00:21:37,946 --> 00:21:39,415
Yeah.

340
00:21:39,948 --> 00:21:44,920
The blood and the traces of a fight we found
at the Beika Apartments when we raced over...

341
00:21:49,325 --> 00:21:52,695
Those were things she had
prepared beforehand.

342
00:21:59,034 --> 00:22:02,237
But, since you were keeping a watch on her...

343
00:22:02,338 --> 00:22:06,075
...you saw everything she had done
to try and camouflage her work...

344
00:22:06,175 --> 00:22:08,977
...at the third apartment while
on the video chat with Ran.

345
00:22:09,278 --> 00:22:12,881
Since she didn't know that
you had found her out...

346
00:22:13,048 --> 00:22:15,918
...Ran went to the
Beika Apartments as planned...

347
00:22:16,752 --> 00:22:18,821
"3rd Apartment"

348
00:22:20,723 --> 00:22:23,592
At that point, she headed for the airport.

349
00:22:23,926 --> 00:22:25,361
But...

350
00:22:34,837 --> 00:22:38,006
"It's better to return the money, right?
Go ahead and take it!"

351
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:42,177
"'Cause without money,
you can't get a woman, can you..."

352
00:22:55,457 --> 00:22:58,026
She was killed by you.

353
00:23:00,562 --> 00:23:05,200
If she was killed here, why did we find her
at those Weekly Apartments in Saitama?

354
00:23:05,267 --> 00:23:08,470
Why did Mizutani-san even rent
that apartment for?

355
00:23:10,038 --> 00:23:13,442
It wasn't Mizutani-san who rented
that Weekly Apartment.

356
00:23:14,810 --> 00:23:16,278
It was you.

357
00:23:18,013 --> 00:23:22,751
You rented that apartment in Mizutani-san's
name because you knew of her plan to escape.

358
00:23:22,885 --> 00:23:25,487
You used the anonymity of
the Internet, didn't you?

359
00:23:25,954 --> 00:23:29,224
"Beika Apartment"
And, you gave the interior of that apartment...

360
00:23:29,324 --> 00:23:31,760
"Saitama Apartment"
...the same setting as the Beika apartment one.

361
00:23:32,294 --> 00:23:36,832
And, having killed Mizutani-san
in the 3rd apartment...

362
00:23:37,232 --> 00:23:40,502
...Kubo-san then went over to
the Beika apartment.

363
00:23:41,537 --> 00:23:43,472
Taking advantage of her prepared play...

364
00:23:43,572 --> 00:23:48,377
...you rushed over to Beika Apartments
so you could bump into Ran.

365
00:23:48,710 --> 00:23:52,181
Having made eye-witness testimony
as to being over there...

366
00:23:52,314 --> 00:23:57,753
...Kubo-san returned to the Weekly Apartments
in Saitama bringing over the corpse and the PC.

367
00:23:57,953 --> 00:24:00,722
Ah, by doing that...

368
00:24:00,823 --> 00:24:05,494
...Kubo-san made it look as if Mizutani-san had been killed
during her video chat at the Saitama Weekly Apartments...

369
00:24:05,627 --> 00:24:09,131
...and since he had been seen at the Beika Apartments,
it would have seemed impossible for him to have done it.

370
00:24:09,231 --> 00:24:10,466
Yes!

371
00:24:10,566 --> 00:24:17,206
Kubo-san had planned the perfect crime by taking
advantage of Mizutani-san's own escape plans.

372
00:24:24,046 --> 00:24:27,616
Even though it was the perfect plan...

373
00:24:28,016 --> 00:24:31,053
How were you able to find me out
from that apartment?

374
00:24:31,520 --> 00:24:33,021
The rug.

375
00:24:33,856 --> 00:24:35,023
The rug?

376
00:24:35,190 --> 00:24:38,227
There was a great deal of blood
found soaked into...

377
00:24:38,494 --> 00:24:40,829
...the rug laid out in the
Saitama Weekly Apartment.

378
00:24:41,196 --> 00:24:45,901
But, though it seemed there should be blood on
the walls and floor, it was only on the rug itself.

379
00:24:46,168 --> 00:24:49,538
When I considered the reasons for that,
there was only one.

380
00:24:49,771 --> 00:24:53,108
That the crime had been performed at
some other place.

381
00:24:53,642 --> 00:24:54,810
But...

382
00:24:54,910 --> 00:24:58,413
...there's no evidence that a body
had been carried away from here...

383
00:24:58,547 --> 00:25:00,649
That's because he didn't carry away
just the corpse.

384
00:25:00,816 --> 00:25:02,651
He also took away the rug.

385
00:25:02,985 --> 00:25:05,487
The one from this 3rd apartment.

386
00:25:19,835 --> 00:25:21,236
From this portion here...

387
00:25:21,436 --> 00:25:25,874
...when connecting it to the rug,
I could see the character "Ku."

388
00:25:27,376 --> 00:25:32,581
Mizutani-san's dying message
was that you were her killer.

389
00:25:42,958 --> 00:25:44,826
Damn!

390
00:25:45,661 --> 00:25:48,463
Even though I had the perfect plan.

391
00:25:49,164 --> 00:25:51,967
Even if you did realize the existence
of a 3rd apartment...

392
00:25:52,034 --> 00:25:54,636
...you shouldn't have been able
to sniff out this apartment!

393
00:25:55,504 --> 00:25:57,673
How did you find out about this apartment?

394
00:25:58,507 --> 00:26:00,075
Easy.

395
00:26:00,275 --> 00:26:03,912
She was killed at 8:16pm.

396
00:26:04,146 --> 00:26:08,684
Ran witnessed you at
Beika Apartments at 8:31pm.

397
00:26:09,217 --> 00:26:13,121
When I hypothesized you had killed
Mizutani-san in some 3rd apartment...

398
00:26:13,388 --> 00:26:18,360
...I knew that 3rd apartment had to be within a
range of 15 minutes from the Beika Apartments.

399
00:26:19,294 --> 00:26:22,197
Furthermore, having to deal with the corpse...

400
00:26:23,532 --> 00:26:24,666
"Heavy!"

401
00:26:25,233 --> 00:26:27,636
"Hey, hey, ow!"

402
00:26:39,047 --> 00:26:42,751
When I verified the time it would take you
to set up your alibi...

403
00:26:42,851 --> 00:26:44,386
...it was 3 hours, 10 minutes.

404
00:26:44,486 --> 00:26:48,123
In other words, because the body
was found 6 hours later...

405
00:26:48,256 --> 00:26:52,227
...the time left for you to move it
was 2 hours and 50 minutes.

406
00:26:52,461 --> 00:26:58,166
When you take a circle of 2 hours 50 minutes
from the Weekly Apartments in Saitama...

407
00:26:58,400 --> 00:27:01,570
...and another circle of 15 minutes from
the Beika Apartments...

408
00:27:01,637 --> 00:27:03,672
...this is where they intersected.

409
00:27:04,272 --> 00:27:08,810
The 3rd apartment had to be in the area
where those two circles intersected.

410
00:27:09,011 --> 00:27:12,447
Moreover, when you zoom in on that area...

411
00:27:13,281 --> 00:27:14,850
Due to a pond being in there...

412
00:27:15,150 --> 00:27:19,187
"Third Apartment"
...there was only this one apartment complex.

413
00:27:28,997 --> 00:27:30,799
I'm not the bad one!

414
00:27:30,899 --> 00:27:33,969
Not at all!
The bad one was that woman!

415
00:27:34,970 --> 00:27:37,639
I loved that woman
from the bottom of my heart!

416
00:27:37,739 --> 00:27:39,875
I didn't intend to kill her!

417
00:27:41,109 --> 00:27:43,178
You say you knew of her betrayal...

418
00:27:43,278 --> 00:27:47,215
...and that you committed your crime
in an unexpected fit of passion.

419
00:27:48,083 --> 00:27:49,584
Kubo-san...

420
00:27:49,851 --> 00:27:52,954
Even so, you calmly planned out
a perfect crime...

421
00:27:53,121 --> 00:27:56,525
...and even meticulously prepared for it
by renting that Weekly Apartment.

422
00:27:56,925 --> 00:28:00,462
Overflowing with malice, you killed her.

423
00:28:00,796 --> 00:28:03,098
You can't talk your way out of that.

424
00:28:10,272 --> 00:28:11,773
Ahh...

425
00:28:12,207 --> 00:28:16,578
I was just tricked and used by
the both of them.

426
00:28:22,718 --> 00:28:23,852
Ran!

427
00:28:23,919 --> 00:28:26,688
Save me, Shin'ichi! Shin...

428
00:28:36,264 --> 00:28:38,900
"Video Chat"

429
00:28:43,772 --> 00:28:45,107
Ran!

430
00:28:51,413 --> 00:28:54,182
"Unknown Caller"

431
00:28:58,153 --> 00:29:02,124
"Time Difference Trick
Hidden in the Elevator"

432
00:29:04,226 --> 00:29:08,897
"Will Shin'ichi Confess to Ran at Last?!"

